  "worked_solution": "Newton\u2019s second law states that\n\n$$\nF=ma,\n$$\n\n \nwhere $F$ is the *resultant* force, $m$ is the mass, and $a$ is the acceleration.\n\nTo compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(t-4)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{3}{t-4},\\,t\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resultant force $F$ at time $t$ equals\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F & =ma \\\\  & =6\\cdot \u27e8\\frac{3}{t-4},\\,t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8\\frac{18}{t-4},\\,6t\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when $t=7\\,\\text{s},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(7) & =\u27e8\\frac{18}{7-4},\\,6(7)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e86,\\,42\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the resultant force acting on $P$ when $t=7\\,\\text{s}$ equals $\u27e86,\\,42\u27e9\\,\\text{N}.$",
